  "case": "default_exports",
  "why": "`module.exports = Base` exports a class as the module's *default*, not as a member called `Base`. A whole-module binding reaches it under any local name (`const B = require('./base'); class Child extends B`), which the reader lost unless the local happened to be spelled `Base`. A destructured `{ Base }` of the same module is `undefined` at run time, and was resolved as though `Base` were a named export.",
